# External NSX App Template

This template shows a standalone NSX app with app-local modules and board content.

## Create

```bash
nsx create-app {{ app_name }} --board {{ board }}
cd {{ app_name }}
```

## Build

```bash
nsx configure --app-dir .
nsx build --app-dir .
{% if sdk_provider == "corstone" %}
```

With the Arm FVP for {{ board }} installed, run the built app:

```bash
nsx run --fvp /path/to/{{ "FVP_Corstone_SSE-320" if board == "corstone320_fvp_u85" else "FVP_Corstone_SSE-300_Ethos-U55" }}
```

{% if board == "corstone320_fvp_u85" %}
On Linux, set the FVP library search path as shown in the
[Corstone target guide](https://ambiqai.github.io/neuralspotx/guides/apps/boards-and-targets/#arm-corstone-virtual-target).
{% endif %}
Omit `--fvp` when the model is on PATH. Each invocation retains the guest UART
and model output under the selected build directory's `nsx-run/` directory.
Expect `nsx hello from generated app` followed by `Application exit code: 0.`
{% else %}
nsx flash --app-dir .
nsx view --app-dir .
```

`nsx view` opens the SEGGER SWO viewer with the board-appropriate reset policy.
Most boards reset after the viewer attaches; Apollo4 secure boards attach
without another reset after `nsx flash`.

Expected SWO output after `flash` + `view`:

```text
nsx hello from generated app
nsx hello from generated app
...
```

{% endif %}
## Layout

- `cmake/nsx/` contains copied NSX CMake support.
- `modules/` contains NSX module sources managed inside this app.
- `boards/` contains the vendored board definition for the selected target.
- `nsx.yml` tracks the app board and enabled module set.
{% if sdk_provider != "corstone" %}
- Use `--reset-on-open` or `--no-reset-on-open` only when you want to override
  the board default.
{% endif %}

If you are using a source checkout instead of a `pipx` install, activate the
`uv` environment first and then run the same `nsx ...` commands.
